e, this is the age where everything hangs in the balance: happiness as well as tragedy. LITTLE AMÉLIE is adapted from the bestseller THE CHARACTER OF RAIN by Amélie Nothomb.","people":["Maïlys Vallade, Liane-Cho Han"],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":100.0,"imageURL":"https://media.grabticks.com/programZD_9344b252-d20f-4312-99d4-db7f1f7807f2.jpg","sourceURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1559","sourceName":"Broadway Cinematheque","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[{"start":"2026-11-28T15:50:00+08:00","version":"French,Japan","bookingURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1559","note":null,"soldOut":false}],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"cin-bcinematheque-all-the-lovers-in-the-night","title":"All the Lovers in the Night","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w160323956","start":"2026-11-28T08:50:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T11:24:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Yukiko Sode · 139 min · Japanese\nFuyuko lives quietly, working as a freelance proofreader, her days largely free of contact with others except for occasional outings with an outgoing colleague. Her only personal ritual is walking alone through the city at midnight on her birthday. A subtle shift begins when she meets Mitsutsuka, a reserved high school physics teacher, at a local culture center. Drawn to his gentle manner and his words, Fuyuko begins meeting him regularly at a café. As their encounters slowly accumulate, a fragile sense of connection takes shape. Yet both carry things they do not easily reveal.\n\nUn Certain Regard, Cannes Film Festival","people":["Yukiko Sode"],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":100.0,"imageURL":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/HK_%E6%B2%B9%E9%BA%BB%E5%9C%B0_Yamatei_near_%E9%A7%BF%E7%99%BC%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%92_Prosperous_Garden_%E7%99%BE%E8%80%81%E5%8C%AF%E9%9B%BB%E5%BD%B1%E4%B8%AD%E5%BF%83_Broadway_Cinematheque_entrance.jpg/960px-HK_%E6%B2%B9%E9%BA%BB%E5%9C%B0_Yamatei_near_%E9%A7%BF%E