rce=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","sourceURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1369","sourceName":"Broadway Cinematheque","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[{"start":"2026-12-05T17:40:00+08:00","version":"German,Danis","bookingURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1369","note":null,"soldOut":false},{"start":"2026-12-18T19:55:00+08:00","version":"German,Danis","bookingURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1369","note":null,"soldOut":false}],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"cin-bcinematheque-i-heard-that-they-are-not-going-to-see-each-other-anymore-special-screening","title":"I HEARD THAT THEY ARE NOT GOING TO SEE EACH OTHER ANYMORE Special Screening","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w160323956","start":"2026-12-05T11:25:00Z","end":"2026-12-05T13:06:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Wong Ka Ki · 86 min · English,Cant\nPresent-day Taipei. Tao, consumed by an inexplicable affection for the indifferent Shin, seeks to preserve their bond through pain. Meanwhile, Melih, a former Istanbul resident running a noodle shop, receives an unexpected flower from the perpetually drunk Ping. As he fixates on the flower, he becomes entangled in Tao's story, reflecting on his own struggles with human connection. Through these intertwined narratives, the film examines the fragility of memory and the ways we attempt to hold onto, or let go of the past.\n\nCPH: DOX\n\nThis special screening comes with a pair of socks.","people":["Wong Ka Ki"],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":130.0,"imageURL":"https://media.grabticks.com/programbF_9c760481-aeaa-47f0-9f82-0e188a9bf028.jpg","sourceURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1622","sourceName":"Broadway Cinematheque","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[{"start":"2026-12-05T19:25:00+08:00","version":"English,Cant","bookingURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1622","note":null,"soldOut":false}],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"cin-bcinematheque-let-s-have-a-cup-of-doodh-patti-chai","title":"Let's have a cup of doodh patti chai","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w160323956","start":"2026-12-06T07:30:00Z","end":"2026-12-06T09:24:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Kwong Yin Brian Hung · 99 min · Cantonese,En\nKam Tin is home to people of many ethnicities, like a miniature United Nations. Chris moves there from the city with his wife Erica and their daughter, Wing Yan. As they adjust to their new life, they must also learn how to get along with neighbours of different ethnicities. Chris starts a business with an Indian partner, though Erica has little faith in it. Wing Yan befriends an African asylum seeker, sparking gossip. Haunted by unpleasant past experiences, Erica carries racial stereotypes, growing increasingly anxious and unsettled as tensions rise… The film has been selected for the main competition section - FIRST International Film Festival (Xining)","people":["Kwong Yin Brian Hung"],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":95.0,"imageURL":"https://media.grabticks.com/programen_57b5500a-0114-4d2d-a255-2d31d1993eb5.jpg","sourceURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/680","sourceName":"Broadway Cinematheque","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[{"start":"2026-12-06T15:30:00+08:00","version":"Cantonese,En","bookingURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/680","note":null,"soldOut":false}],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"cin-bcinematheque-banzai","title":"Banzaï","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w160323956","start":"2026-12-06T09:00:00Z","end":"2026-12-06T11:07:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Claude Zidi · 112 min · French,Arabi\nMichel Bernardin works for “Planet Assistance”, which helps travellers in need. On his first assignment, Michel goes to North Africa to get a man out of the hospital but ends up with the wrong man and accidentally sets off a coup d’état. In New York, he is attacked by men in Harlem\nwhile trying to bring a musician back. Lastly, he goes to Hong Kong, where he comes across his fiancée but is also an unwitting puppet of some racketeers.","people":["Claude Zidi"],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":95.0,"imageURL":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/HK_%E6%B2%B9%E9%BA%BB%E5%9C%B0_Yamatei_near_%E9%A7%BF%E7%99%BC%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%92_Prosperous_Garden_%E7%99%BE%E8%80%81%E5%8C%AF%E9%9B%BB%E5%BD%B1%E4%B8%AD%E5%BF%83_Broadway_Cinematheque_entrance.jpg/960px-HK_%E6%B2%B9%E9%BA%BB%E5%9C%B0_Yamatei_near_%E9%A7%BF%E7%99%BC%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%92_Prosperous_Garden_%E7%99%BE%E8%80%81%E5%8C%AF%E9%9B%BB%E5%BD%B1%E4%B8%AD%E5%BF%83_Broadway_Cinematheque_entrance.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","sourceURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1470","sourceName":"Broadway Cinematheque","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[{"start":"2026-12-06T17:00:00+08:00","version":"French,Arabi","bookingURL":"https://www.cinema.com.hk/en/movie/1470","note":null,"soldOut":false}],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"cin-bcinematheque-orange-flavoured-wedding","title":"Orange Flavoured Wedding","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w160323956","start":"2026-12-06T11:15:00Z","end":"2026-12-06T13:25:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Christophe Honoré · 115 min · French\nIt is March 1978 in the suburbs of Nantes. The Puig family has seven children, and today is the wedding of the youngest: Jacques. The father is not attending the wedding; he has been banished from the family. The brothers and sisters, however, are all there, happy to be reunited. Jacques is marrying Martine. For the two of them, it’s a marriage of love. But can love heal the wounds of childhood?","people":["Christophe Honoré"],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":95.0,"imageURL":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo